{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/6349-wild-setting-speculation","id":6349,"title":"Wild Setting Speculation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-08T14:37:14-08:00","id":6349,"title":"Wild Setting Speculation","content":"So, since we're so far out from the scheduled release that they only have an outline for the core book, why don't we waste some time speculating? Ian has indicated that he has plans for at least two more settings that also have names that begin with 'A.' Any ideas when those might be, or what they might be called? I assume that one is probably a future setting even further out than Aeon. The other is where I get stuck. I figure it is ether set in ancient times (maybe that's the setting name &quot;Ancient&quot;), or maybe WWII or in the 70's (to deal with that old timeline entry).<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?<br /> <br /> -Slag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T18:27:59-08:00","id":6519,"title":"","content":"Age of Reason? Age of Arthur? Both have a feel to them that could be told with the system, The 70's could easily be handled with the new core &quot;Modern setting just need to handle the tech level issues...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T20:47:03-08:00","id":6586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/6349-wild-setting-speculation#post6349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ian has indicated that he has plans for at least two more settings that also have names that begin with 'A.'</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://twitter.com/VonAether/status/355100638209777667\" target=\"_blank\">Four</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/6349-wild-setting-speculation?p=6519#post6519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Age of Reason? Age of Arthur?</div> </div> </div> </div>None of the new settings start with &quot;Age of...&quot; I like to think we're a little more creative than that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T21:22:18-08:00","id":6604,"title":"","content":"I didn't have my first cup of coffee yet. I'll also admit that the Age of Reason/ Enlightenment is the era I'm currently writing a chronicle for so it is on my mind. Arthur the once and future King. America The Rise of the Revolution. Andalusia the Reconquonista. Sorry I have only had one cup of coffee that is about all I can think of at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T22:45:46-08:00","id":6644,"title":"","content":"Aegis (Classical era - was tempted by 'Antiquity', but decided it'd probably be something in Classical Greek)<br /> Aether (Victorian era)<br /> Allies (WW2)<br /> Action! (70s)<br /> Aberrant War<br /> <br /> (Why yes, there are more than four.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T00:50:05-08:00","id":6677,"title":"","content":"Also, for even earlier in the classical era, you could have Argonauts! since The Argonautica (aka Jason and the Argonauts) is after all one of the earliest stories of a band of heroes (ie PCs) going on adventures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","name":"John Snead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar96_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T05:52:58-08:00","id":6766,"title":"","content":"Antiquity (Ages Long Past)<br /> Ascension (Even farther in the future, or maybe the past...)<br /> Atlantis (cause it worked so well for Disney and Mage :P)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T05:57:41-08:00","id":6768,"title":"","content":"That brings us up to eight, right? The four in the core books (<b>Trinity Continuum</b>, <b>Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on</b>, <b>Trinity Continuum: Aberrant</b>, and <b>Trinity Continuum: Adventure!</b>), plus four more? Or is the modern-day Action heroes setting in the core book one of those four more? <br /> <br /> World War II is definitely one I\u2019d like to see. I\u2019d also like to see a Victorian-Age one, though if <b>Adventure!</b> retains its status of \u201cwhere it all started\u201d that could be tricky. I\u2019d also like to see a post-Process-418 one designed as an opposite bookend from <b>Adventure!</b> that likewise features a mix of psychics, superhumans, and talents; but I\u2019d like to see it pushed further into the future to give <b>\u00c6on</b> more breathing room. And I\u2019d like one set between the end of the Aberrant War and the rise of the Psi Orders, depicting a somewhat harder sci-fi era than <b>\u00c6on</b> covers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T12:04:29-08:00","id":6958,"title":"","content":"This doesn't stike me as a pure hard Sci Fi rule set (but then I don't really know what is). I'd like a far future Space Opera setting. Make it a setting where humanity is recovering from a <b><i>Long Night</i></b>/<b><i>Dark Ages</i></b> and have the PCs searching for lost human colonies. this would let you do any type of adventure story the rule set would support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T18:47:49-08:00","id":10121,"title":"","content":"Action! was a title I used for a home brew Adventure! game that took place in the Cold War 1980's. I took inspiration from the Stallone and Schwarzenegger action movies of the era. I wrote some material but never got to actually run it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T17:41:14-08:00","id":11729,"title":"","content":"If it's &quot;Action&quot; I demand to play a Blaxploitation character. His name will be &quot;Thunder Brown&quot; and he'll carry a huge ass gun. His Afro will act as head armor. none of that jerry curl nonsense. He will raise his fist at the end of every session and say &quot;Solid&quot; ....I WANT THIS GAME RIGHT NOW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/238-hammerofheaven","name":"HammerofHeaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar238_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T23:22:23-08:00","id":11918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HammerofHeaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/6349-wild-setting-speculation?p=11729#post11729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's &quot;Action&quot; I demand to play a Blaxploitation character. His name will be &quot;Thunder Brown&quot; and he'll carry a huge ass gun. His Afro will act as head armor. none of that jerry curl nonsense. He will raise his fist at the end of every session and say &quot;Solid&quot; ....I WANT THIS GAME RIGHT NOW.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;<a href=\"http://www.rpg.net/reviews/archive/11/11119.phtml\" target=\"_blank\">Solid! The Blaxploitation RPG</a>&quot; is a thing that exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T23:48:57-08:00","id":11928,"title":"","content":"I'll refrain from disparaging systems remarks here, but that's not a system I'd use to represent the type of hero i want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/238-hammerofheaven","name":"HammerofHeaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar238_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T02:22:52-08:00","id":13882,"title":"","content":"<u>I speculate that:</u> The Qin will have dinosaur-biosuit that are vehicle and walker sized! with lazerz pew pew... and other alien goodies. Like acid canons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T08:55:12-08:00","id":14085,"title":"","content":"Wow, light-hero, I know I said &quot;wild,&quot; but you really took the ball and ran <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Though, more mech suits is usually a good move, I once got an Adventure! game off the ground with the promise of Apes piloting mechs.<br /> <br /> -Slag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T10:38:44-08:00","id":14158,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PkmFv.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T10:42:01-08:00","id":14161,"title":"","content":"I'd play that game...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/324-ardenty","name":"ardenty","avatar":"https://forum.t